{"id":"dfd5be6f22b3deb4","group":"58","path":"58/batch16/58-prop-riesz-representation.md","title":"Riesz Representation Theorem","display":"prop-riesz-representation — Riesz Representation Theorem","type":"proposition","metadata":{"type":"proposition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-prop-riesz-representation","aliases":["58-prop-riesz-representation"],"display":"prop-riesz-representation — Riesz Representation Theorem","depends_on":["[[58-df-hilbert-space]]","[[58-df-bounded-linear]]","[[58-df-operator-norm]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"proposition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-prop-riesz-representation"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-prop-riesz-representation</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"prop-riesz-representation — Riesz Representation Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"b70ce791d5b1a19b\" href=\"?note=b70ce791d5b1a19b\" title=\"58-df-hilbert-space\">58-df-hilbert-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"261de7e0269cd7e2\" href=\"?note=261de7e0269cd7e2\" title=\"58-df-bounded-linear\">58-df-bounded-linear</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"28f93ddcd4761c3f\" href=\"?note=28f93ddcd4761c3f\" title=\"58-df-operator-norm\">58-df-operator-norm</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\">\\(\\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H,B,+_H,\\odot_H,f\\in V\">\\(H,B,+_H,\\odot_H,f\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"+_{\\mathbb K},\\cdot_{\\mathbb K}\">\\(+_{\\mathbb K},\\cdot_{\\mathbb K}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|\\cdot|_{\\mathbb K}\">\\(|\\cdot|_{\\mathbb K}\\)</span> (the standard scalar addition, multiplication, and absolute-value norm)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\nu_B(x)\\coloneqq\\sqrt{B(x,x)}\">\\(\\nu_B(x)\\coloneqq\\sqrt{B(x,x)}\\)</span> (the norm induced by the inner product)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B,\\mathbb K,+_H,\\odot_H)\">\\(\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B,\\mathbb K,+_H,\\odot_H)\\)</span> (fully explicit Hilbert-space predicate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BoundedLinear}_S(f,H,\\mathbb K,\\mathbb K,+_H,\\odot_H,+_{\\mathbb K},\\cdot_{\\mathbb K},\\nu_B,|\\cdot|_{\\mathbb K})\">\\(\\mathrm{BoundedLinear}_S(f,H,\\mathbb K,\\mathbb K,+_H,\\odot_H,+_{\\mathbb K},\\cdot_{\\mathbb K},\\nu_B,|\\cdot|_{\\mathbb K})\\)</span> (fully explicit bounded-linear predicate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{OperatorNorm}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{OperatorNorm}_S\\)</span> (operator-norm value predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"28f93ddcd4761c3f\" href=\"?note=28f93ddcd4761c3f\" title=\"58-df-operator-norm\">58-df-operator-norm</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{prop\\text{-}riesz\\text{-}representation}\\vdash\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B,\\mathbb K,+_H,\\odot_H)\\land\\mathrm{BoundedLinear}_S(f,H,\\mathbb K,\\mathbb K,+_H,\\odot_H,+_{\\mathbb K},\\cdot_{\\mathbb K},\\nu_B,|\\cdot|_{\\mathbb K})\\to\\exists!y\\in H\\;\\Bigl(\\forall x\\in H\\;(f(x)=B(x,y))\\land\\exists r\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{OperatorNorm}_S(r,f,H,\\mathbb K,\\mathbb K,+_H,+_{\\mathbb K},\\odot_H,\\cdot_{\\mathbb K},\\nu_B,|\\cdot|_{\\mathbb K})\\land r=\\nu_B(y)\\bigr)\\Bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{prop\\text{-}riesz\\text{-}representation}\\vdash\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B,\\mathbb K,+_H,\\odot_H)\\land\\mathrm{BoundedLinear}_S(f,H,\\mathbb K,\\mathbb K,+_H,\\odot_H,+_{\\mathbb K},\\cdot_{\\mathbb K},\\nu_B,|\\cdot|_{\\mathbb K})\\to\\exists!y\\in H\\;\\Bigl(\\forall x\\in H\\;(f(x)=B(x,y))\\land\\exists r\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{OperatorNorm}_S(r,f,H,\\mathbb K,\\mathbb K,+_H,+_{\\mathbb K},\\odot_H,\\cdot_{\\mathbb K},\\nu_B,|\\cdot|_{\\mathbb K})\\land r=\\nu_B(y)\\bigr)\\Bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The formula adopts the convention that the inner product is linear in its first argument.</li>\n<li>The scalar field, vector operations, induced norm, and operator-norm value are explicit; no hidden compatibility projection supplies them.</li>\n<li>Over <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb C\">\\(\\mathbb C\\)</span>, the representing map <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"y\\mapsto\\langle\\,\\cdot\\,,y\\rangle\">\\(y\\mapsto\\langle\\,\\cdot\\,,y\\rangle\\)</span> is a conjugate-linear isometric bijection; over <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R\">\\(\\mathbb R\\)</span> it is linear.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-hilbert-space","status":"resolved","id":"b70ce791d5b1a19b","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-hilbert-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-bounded-linear","status":"resolved","id":"261de7e0269cd7e2","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-bounded-linear]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-operator-norm","status":"resolved","id":"28f93ddcd4761c3f","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-operator-norm]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-operator-norm","status":"resolved","id":"28f93ddcd4761c3f","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{OperatorNorm}_S$ (operator-norm value predicate, see [[58-df-operator-norm]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}","display":false},{"tex":"H,B,+_H,\\odot_H,f\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"+_{\\mathbb K},\\cdot_{\\mathbb K}","display":false},{"tex":"|\\cdot|_{\\mathbb K}","display":false},{"tex":"\\nu_B(x)\\coloneqq\\sqrt{B(x,x)}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B,\\mathbb K,+_H,\\odot_H)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{BoundedLinear}_S(f,H,\\mathbb K,\\mathbb K,+_H,\\odot_H,+_{\\mathbb K},\\cdot_{\\mathbb K},\\nu_B,|\\cdot|_{\\mathbb K})","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{OperatorNorm}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{prop\\text{-}riesz\\text{-}representation}\\vdash\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B,\\mathbb K,+_H,\\odot_H)\\land\\mathrm{BoundedLinear}_S(f,H,\\mathbb K,\\mathbb K,+_H,\\odot_H,+_{\\mathbb K},\\cdot_{\\mathbb K},\\nu_B,|\\cdot|_{\\mathbb K})\\to\\exists!y\\in H\\;\\Bigl(\\forall x\\in H\\;(f(x)=B(x,y))\\land\\exists r\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{OperatorNorm}_S(r,f,H,\\mathbb K,\\mathbb K,+_H,+_{\\mathbb K},\\odot_H,\\cdot_{\\mathbb K},\\nu_B,|\\cdot|_{\\mathbb K})\\land r=\\nu_B(y)\\bigr)\\Bigr).","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathbb C","display":false},{"tex":"y\\mapsto\\langle\\,\\cdot\\,,y\\rangle","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R","display":false}],"bytes":1934,"backlinks":[{"id":"bcd498adc92fd397","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-3990","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-prop-riesz-representation.md|58-prop-riesz-representation]]（batch16）"}],"outgoing":["b70ce791d5b1a19b","261de7e0269cd7e2","28f93ddcd4761c3f"]}